There are lines that we have not discussed, such as tPull lines which pull text from other forms.
These as you can see have fields that indicate the form, copy and line from which to pull.

There is one abnormality in our file that needs to be corrected.
The first column named data does not contain any lines.
As we noted before, the compiler will not tolerate this situation.

The purpose of this first column is to enclose all the data boxes on the form
so that they can be moved on one, up or down as needed.
In my experience the y values obtained from Gimp are about 0.10 inches too low.
This column allows one to move all the boxes up 0.10in in one fell swoop.

To do this move the line Endcol**************
from below the first col to the end of the page
just before the line EndPgF

You should place this enclosing column on each of your subsequent pages.
copy

xcol    	!2name   	!3top    	!4align                        !5left           !6right  
col     	!data    	!0.00    	!left			       !0.00		!8.50    

to the beginning of each page right after the PgM or PgL lines and

Endcol****************

to the end of each page just be for the EndpgM*** or EndpgL***** lines.

